  "note": "Valid, but every right side is +∞ because |(h−h_H)/t|_∞ = ∞ (see (A.36)); the notation |(h−h_H(t))/t|_∞ mixes a function with its value (harmless). The book needs the log t and 1/t versions only in Prop 9.5.1, which Lean proves by Mellin/Plancherel bounds (prop_9_5_1, MajorArcs/Prop715.lean:300)."
